{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0097207","isObsolete":false,"name":"bud dormancy process","definition":{"text":"A dormancy process in which dormancy (sometimes called a dormant state) is induced, maintained or broken in a bud. Bud dormancy is a suspension of most physiological activity and growth that can be reactivated. It may be a response to environmental conditions such as seasonality or extreme heat, drought, or cold. The exit from bud dormancy is marked by the resumed growth of the bud.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PO_REF","dbId":"00009"}]},"comment":"Bud dormancy may precede dormancy of the whole plant.","synonyms":[{"name":"bud dormancy","type":"related"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044767 (single-organism developmental process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044707 (single-multicellular organism process)"},{"timestamp":"2017-08-13","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0032501 (multicellular organismal process)"},{"timestamp":"2015-12-09","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-28","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044767 (single-organism developmental process)"},{"timestamp":"2012-12-15","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044707 (single-multicellular organism process)"},{"timestamp":"2012-01-06","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"bud dormancy process"},{"timestamp":"2012-01-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"bud dormancy"},{"timestamp":"2012-01-06","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A dormancy process in which dormancy (sometimes called a dormant state) is induced, maintained or broken in a bud. Bud dormancy is a suspension of most physiological activity and growth that can be reactivated. It may be a response to environmental conditions such as seasonality or extreme heat, drought, or cold. The exit from bud dormancy is marked by the resumed growth of the bud."},{"timestamp":"2012-01-06","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0022611 (dormancy process)"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0097207","ancestorName":"bud dormancy process","relationship":"only_in_taxon","taxId":"33090","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Viridiplantae"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted"}],"pageInfo":null}